import Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.UniversalEnveloping
import Langlands.Representation.Archimedean.RealGenericLargeReduction

/-!
# Kostant's Whittaker theorem for finite products of `𝔤𝔩_n(ℂ)`

`GLProductWhittakerMaximallyFaithfulStatement` is Kostant's theorem (Kostant 1978,
Theorem 3.9 = Theorem D) for the complex reductive Lie algebra
`𝔤 = ∏_{i ∈ ι} 𝔤𝔩_{n_i}(ℂ)`, with `ι` finite: a `𝔤`-module with an infinitesimal character
whose algebraic dual contains a nonzero Whittaker vector for a non-singular character of the
blockwise strictly upper triangular subalgebra is maximally faithful.

The Lie algebra is the type `∀ i, Matrix (Fin (n i)) (Fin (n i)) ℂ` of tuples of matrices,
with the commutator bracket of its pointwise product. The predicates `HasInfinitesimalCharacter`
and `IsMaximallyFaithful` are those of `RealGenericLargeReduction`.

The case `ι = Unit` covers `ℂ ⊗_ℝ 𝔤𝔩_n(ℝ) ≅ 𝔤𝔩_n(ℂ)` and the case `ι = Fin 2` covers
`ℂ ⊗_ℝ 𝔤𝔩_n(ℂ) ≅ 𝔤𝔩_n(ℂ) × 𝔤𝔩_n(ℂ)`.
-/

noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace Langlands.Archimedean

attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing

universe uV

/-- Kostant's theorem (1978, Theorem 3.9 = Theorem D) for the finite product
`∏_{i ∈ ι} 𝔤𝔩_{n_i}(ℂ)`. Let `π` be a Lie algebra map from the tuples of matrices
`∀ i, Matrix (Fin (n i)) (Fin (n i)) ℂ` (commutator bracket) to `End(V)` with an infinitesimal
character. Let `ℓ` be a nonzero linear functional on `V` and let `a i p` be complex numbers, with
`a i p ≠ 0` whenever `p + 1 < n i`. Assume that every blockwise strictly upper triangular `X`
satisfies `ℓ(π(X) v) = (∑ᵢ ∑ₚ a i p · X i p (p+1)) ℓ(v)` for all `v`, so `ℓ` is a nonzero
Whittaker vector in the full dual of `V` for a non-singular character. Then `π` is maximally
faithful: its annihilator in the enveloping algebra is generated by its central elements. -/
def GLProductWhittakerMaximallyFaithfulStatement : Prop :=
  ∀ (ι : Type) [Fintype ι] (n : ι → ℕ) (V : Type uV) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V]
    (π : (∀ i, Matrix (Fin (n i)) (Fin (n i)) ℂ) →ₗ⁅ℂ⁆ Module.End ℂ V),
    HasInfinitesimalCharacter π →
    ∀ ℓ : V →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ, ℓ ≠ 0 →
    ∀ a : ∀ i, Fin (n i) → ℂ, (∀ (i : ι) (p : Fin (n i)), (p : ℕ) + 1 < n i → a i p ≠ 0) →
      (∀ X : ∀ i, Matrix (Fin (n i)) (Fin (n i)) ℂ,
          (∀ (i : ι) (p q : Fin (n i)), (q : ℕ) ≤ p → X i p q = 0) →
          ∀ v : V, ℓ (π X v) =
            (∑ i : ι, ∑ p : Fin (n i), ∑ q : Fin (n i),
              if (q : ℕ) = p + 1 then a i p * X i p q else 0) * ℓ v) →
      IsMaximallyFaithful π

end Langlands.Archimedean
